                <pb facs="0785" n="705" sameAs="frus:frus1902/pg705"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Buck to Mr.
                            Hay.</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.—Paraphrase.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Tokyo</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1902-03-17"><hi rendition="#italic">March 17,
                        1902</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>(Mr. Buck reports that a proposal to arbitrate has been made by the Japanese
                    Government to the representatives of the powers protesting; that the United
                    States, not having protested, is not included, and inquires whether it would be
                    proper to ask that the United States Government be made a party to the
                    arbitration.)</p>
            </div>
        </body>
